comment.narrative:
0. At least 1 experiment is successfully designed and developed from idea stage to MVP and find its wide practical application
#50,000 users in the CIS countries learning the programming, and attending the BalaTech Olympiad.
1.	Develop at least two experiments with the use of innovative data for specific fields 1. mudslides and flooding prediction 2. misogyny prevention and test the hypothesis about the applicability of AI and machine learning as a part of implementation of Data for Development initiative; Share lessons, insights and knowledge with respective colleagues; integrate results of experiments into UNDP programming to advance the use of the state-of-the-art technologies;
2.	Promote digital agenda and build capacity of the UNDP CO to better use digital to amplify UNDP’s impact and implement “digital by default” principle;
3.	Build partnership with local startups and global startup ecosystem to support local startups led by youth and women;
4.	Explore and conceptualize at least one innovative way to territorial development and use innovative approaches to foster their implementation;
5.	Conceptualize and launch at least one dialogue platform to support the development of local creators and promote mutually reinforcing collaborations; 
6.	Raise awareness about creative economy and future of jobs with the focus on women and youth;
7.	Explore gaps in skills, knowledge and capacities hampering youth in learning professional skills and getting jobs in creative industries; 
8.	Design, develop and prototype digital tourism product in collaboration with the Osh Mayor’s Office;
9.	Test the concept of the Women Creative Lab in Osh, collect knowledge and insights, improve the paradigm and scale it to other locations;
10.	Design and develop a draft project document on the development of creative ecosystem in Kyrgyzstan
11. Launch of online crowdfunding platform (wclkg.org)

1.	Two experiments on DATA INNOVATION FOR DEVELOPMENT were designed: 1.1. test the use of machine learning and AI in the field of mudslides and flooding prediction via combination of satellite and historical data (DRM) 1.2. test the use of machine learning for identifying hate speech toward women using data from social media
2.	Digital Agenda at the CO was promoted through close collaboration with the Chief Digital Office. UNDP Kyrgyzstan became the first CO in the world receiving Digital Fitness Programme (DFP) offline. DFP is a short, intensive course facilitated by CDO, designed for CO Leadership and Program Teams to help COs better use digital to amplify their impact. 
3.	In 2022 UNDP became official partner of the CODIFY IT group of companies and She Loves Tech global platform committed to closing the funding gap for women entrepreneurs, and building an ecosystem for technology, entrepreneurship, and innovation that creates opportunities for women. More than 80 startup applications were collected at the regional level; 10 startups pitched their ideas, one startup was given an opportunity to pitch at the global level.
4.	The concept of the creative placemaking as an innovative approach to regional and territorial development was explored; the methodology of “eventful places” were introduced into UNDP programming;
5.	CREATE4, a unique platform for the development and support of the creative community of Kyrgyzstan was designed and organized by UNDP in the Kyrgyz Republic and Association of Creative Industries of Kyrgyzstan (ACI). 
6.	More than 3000 youths offline and around 2000 online learned about creative economy from the leading practitioners and successful role models;
7.	Research for assessing the gaps hampering youths in learning professions has been conceptualized;
8.	All content, UX-UI design and prototype of the digital tourism product were developed;
9.	The concept of the WCL was tested successfully in Osh; two more labs have been launched in Batken and Jalal-Abad;
10.	Draft project document on the development of creative ecosystem in Kyrgyzstan has been developed
11. Crowdfunding platform was developed and launched (wclkg.org)
